## Migration safety rules

Before applying any migration:

1. Inspect the existing schema and migration history.
2. Identify destructive operations and data dependencies.
3. Preserve existing user accounts, uploads, purchases and financial records.
4. Back up the database when the environment permits.
5. Use additive or backward-compatible migrations whenever possible.
6. Test migrations against a disposable development database or database snapshot.
7. Validate data integrity before and after migration.
8. Provide rollback or recovery instructions.
9. Never reset, drop or recreate a production database merely to make the new schema work.
10. Never delete real user data to accommodate a new schema.

Use explicit transactions where supported. For schema operations that MySQL cannot safely roll back, use a documented expand-and-contract migration strategy.

Seed only required reference data, such as predefined roles and initial categories. Do not insert fake users, paid purchases, creator earnings or successful payment records into production.

